pitalar_na_regi%C3%A3o_do_rio_Japur%C3%A1_e_Solim%C3%B5es,_em_munic%C3%ADpios_do_Amazonas_-_2023_(53262317396).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=140445826","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Durante a Opera\u00e7\u00e3o \u00c1gata Norte , o navio de Assist\u00eancia Hospitalar Oswaldo Cruz  atendeu os munic\u00edpios de Fonte Boa, Uarini, Alvar\u00e3es, Codaj\u00e1s e Anori, os quais decretaram estado de emerg\u00eancia devido a crise causada pela seca dos rios amaz\u00f4nicos. Foram realizados 1.000 atendimentos e distribu\u00eddos mais de 30 mil medicamentos nesses munic\u00edpios.\n</p>\nAl\u00e9m dos atendimentos m\u00e9dicos, tamb\u00e9m foram realizadas palestras educativas sobre higiene bucal e distribu\u00eddos kits de higiene bucal e medicamentos para a popula\u00e7\u00e3o ribeirinha.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/57999093@N04\">Marinha do Brasil</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"125606949":{"pageid":125606949,"ns":6,"title":"File:O Nheengatu, entre a vida e a morte \u2014 a tradu\u00e7\u00e3o liter\u00e1ria como poss\u00edvel instrumento de sua revitaliza\u00e7\u00e3o lexical.pdf","index":5,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":497609,"width":1239,"height":1752,"pagecount":21,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/O_Nheengatu%2C_entre_a_vida_e_a_morte_%E2%80%94_a_tradu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_liter%C3%A1ria_como_poss%C3%ADvel_instrumento_de_sua_revitaliza%C3%A7%C3%A3o_lexical.pdf/page1-960px-O_Nheengatu%2C_entre_a_vida_e_a_morte_%E2%80%94_a_tradu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_liter%C3%A1ria_como_poss%C3%ADvel_instrumento_de_sua_revitaliza%C3%A7%C3%A3o_lexical.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":905,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/O_Nheengatu%2C_entre_a_vida_e_a_morte_%E2%80%94_a_tradu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_liter%C3%A1ria_como_poss%C3%ADvel_instrumento_de_sua_revitaliza%C3%A7%C3%A3o_lexical.pdf/page1-960px-O_Nheengatu%2C_entre_a_vida_e_a_morte_%E2%80%94_a_tradu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_liter%C3%A1ria_como_poss%C3%ADvel_instrumento_de_sua_revitaliza%C3%A7%C3%A3o_lexical.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":905},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/O_Nheengatu%2C_entre_a_vida_e_a_morte_%E2%80%94_a_tradu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_liter%C3%A1ria_como_poss%C3%ADvel_instrumento_de_sua_revitaliza%C3%A7%C3%A3o_lexical.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O_Nheengatu,_entre_a_vida_e_a_morte_%E2%80%94_a_tradu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_liter%C3%A1ria_como_poss%C3%ADvel_instrumento_de_sua_revitaliza%C3%A7%C3%A3o_lexical.pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=125606949","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Eduardo_de_Almeida_Navarro\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Eduardo de Almeida Navarro\"><span title=\"Brazilian philologist and lexicographer\">Eduardo de Almeida Navarro</span></a></bdi> / <bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q136335446\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q136335446\"><span title=\"Brazilian linguist\">Marcel Twardowsky Avila</span></a></bdi> / <bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q136335453\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q136335453\"><span title=\"Brazilian linguist\">Rodrigo Godinho Trevisan</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Nheengatu historically developed from Amazonian L\u00edngua Geral and is still spoken in Amazonia by about 6000 people, and has a great historical relevance for having been the most employed language in that South American region, not only in Brazil, but also in Colombia and Venezuela. During the Rubber Cycle, between 1870 and 1910, Nheengatu was surpassed by Portuguese because of migration of workers coming from Northeastern Brazil, in search for employment in rubber plantations of that region. As it became increasingly endangered, Nheengatu was given a grammar, a dictionary and a literature, which represents an important source of linguistic information for present initiatives towards its revitalization. Some of them are literary translations by postgraduates in Translation Studies Program in S\u00e3o Paulo University. Such attempts may help to revitalize Nheengatu lexicon, avoiding overuse of Portuguese words, a factor of weakening of that Amazonian language.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"164023623":{"pageid":164023623,"ns":6,"title":"File:Queimadas - Lago Coari (AM).jpg","index":6,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":30317,"width":940,"height":604,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/Queimadas_-_Lago_Coari_%28AM%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":411,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/Queimadas_-_Lago_Coari_%28AM%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":411},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/Queimadas_-_Lago_Coari_%28AM%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queimadas_-_Lago_Coari_(AM).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=164023623","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Fotografia autoral que mostra focos de queimada, no horizo